the add two numbers for a number N with a number M is a number K if
    K = N + M.

the multiply two numbers for a number N with a number M is a number K if
    K = N * M.

the sum of three numbers for a number N with a number M with a number K is a number P if
    P = N + M + K.

the get x coordinate for a point is the x of the point.

the delta x for a point with a second point is a number N if
    the x of the second point is a number M
    and the x of the point is a number K
    and N = M - K.

the delta y for a point with a second point is a number N if
    the y of the second point is a number M
    and the y of the point is a number K
    and N = M - K.

the distance squared between points for a point with a second point is a number N if
    the delta x for the point with the second point is a number M
    and the delta x for the point with the second point is a number K
    and the delta y for the point with the second point is a number P
    and the delta y for the point with the second point is a number Q
    and N = M * K + P * Q.

